## Decision Log
### 2026-07-27 — Remove claude-mem hard dependency; make Handoff fully self-contained
- **Context:** Handoff V2 had 4 hard references to claude-mem with no fallback. Users without claude-mem couldn't run the skill reliably.
- **Decision:** Add inline guards at every touchpoint — "If available... else skip silently." claude-mem becomes an optional enhancement.
- **Why:** Skill must work perfectly on its own. External tools are complementary, not required.
- **Rejected:** Plugin architecture (YAGNI — only one optional dependency).

### 2026-07-26 — V2 dual-file model over V1 single-file
- **Context:** V1 overwrote the entire handoff each time, losing decisions and lessons across sessions.
- **Decision:** PROJECT.ftmd (persistent, append-mode) + HANDOFF.ftmd (session snapshot, archived after read).
- **Why:** Decisions and failures accumulate; session snapshots are disposable. Separating them prevents information loss.
- **Rejected:** Single file with append (bloated), SQLite (overkill).

### 2026-07-26 — 7-step sync checklist for every skill update
- **Context:** Multiple inconsistencies found between .claude, Desktop repo, and GitHub — version numbers, format descriptions, repo description.
- **Decision:** Mandatory 7-step (now 7+1) checklist executed after every SKILL.md change.
- **Why:** Three locations with different purposes are easy to desync. Explicit checklist beats memory.
- **Rejected:** Auto-sync script (too rigid, some steps need human judgment).

## Failure Memory
### 2026-07-27 — Version badge not updated during V2.3 release
- **Attempt:** Committed V2.3 changes, pushed tag, created release — but README badge still said v2.2.0.
- **Result:** Badge and release tag mismatched until栋老师 asked for final check.
- **Root cause:** 7-step checklist item #3 said "version number" but didn't explicitly call out the badge URL.
- **Lesson:** Added "grep old version numbers across all .md files" as the +1 step. Badge URL is the most frequently missed item.

